"Saudi Traffic Directorate sets 6 conditions for heavy trucks on roads - Latest News from Saudi Arabia and the World (https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/664512/saudi-arabia/saudi-traffic-directorate-sets-6-conditions-for-heavy-trucks-on-roads)\nciteturn8search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: yesterday; # Saudi Traffic Directorate sets 6 conditions for heavy trucks on roads ... The General Directorate of Traffic in Saudi Arabia has mandated six conditions for truck and heavy equipment drivers while their vehicles are traveling on roads.\n\n# Saudi Traffic Directorate sets 6 conditions for heavy trucks on roads\n\nSeptember 12, 2026 | 06:54 PM\n\nThe General Directorate of Traffic in Saudi Arabia has mandated six conditions for truck and heavy equipment drivers while their vehicles are traveling on roads.\n\nSeptember 12, 2026 | 06:54 PM\n\nSaudi Gazette report  \n\nLast Updated: September 12, 2026 | 06:54 PM\n\nImage\n\n3 minute read\n\nA A\n\nResize\n\nImage: increase-icon\n\nRIYADH — The General Directorate of Traffic in Saudi Arabia has mandated six conditions for truck and heavy equipment drivers while their vehicles are traveling on roads.\n\nFirstly, truck drivers are required to use the rightmost lane on multi-lane roads. Secondly, they should adhere to the permitted times for entering or exiting cities. It is also stipulated that transported loads must be securely covered and fastened to prevent them from falling.\n\nThe drivers are prohibited from transporting passengers in trucks not designed for that purpose. It is also mandated that drivers have to place a triangular warning sign or reflector at a sufficient distance behind the truck when it is stopped at night. Sixthly, they should comply with the permitted dimensions and weight limits for loads to avoid violations and hazards.\n\nThe directorate emphasized that truck drivers’ compliance with traffic regulations and instructions is a fundamental element in enhancing road safety and protecting all road users. It also states that implementing the announced regulations is a shared responsibility between drivers and regulatory authorities.\n\nThe directorate considers compliance with these requirements the first line of defense in reducing the risks associated with truck traffic. It also contributes to raising the level of traffic discipline and achieving the highest standards of public safety on the roads.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSaudi Traffic Directorate sets 6 conditions for heavy trucks on roads (https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/625590)\nciteturn8search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.0 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; Saudi Traffic Directorate sets 6 conditions for heavy trucks on roadsImage: The General Directorate of Traffic in Saudi Arabia has mandated six conditions for truck and heavy equipment drivers while their vehicles are traveling on roads.\n\nSAUDI ARABIA\n\nSaudi Traffic Directorate sets 6 conditions for heavy trucks on roads\n\nImage: The General Directorate of Traffic in Saudi Arabia has mandated six conditions for truck and heavy equipment drivers while their vehicles are traveling on roads.\n\nRIYADH — The General Directorate of Traffic in Saudi Arabia has mandated six conditions for truck and heavy equipment drivers while their vehicles are traveling on roads.\n\nFirstly, truck drivers are required to use the rightmost lane on multi-lane roads. Secondly, they should adhere to the permitted times for entering or exiting cities. It is also stipulated that transported loads must be securely covered and fastened to prevent them from falling.\n\nThe drivers are prohibited from transporting passengers in trucks not designed for that purpose. It is also mandated that drivers have to place a triangular warning sign or reflector at a sufficient distance behind the truck when it is stopped at night. Sixthly, they should comply with the permitted dimensions and weight limits for loads to avoid violations and hazards.\n\nThe directorate emphasized that truck drivers’ compliance with traffic regulations and instructions is a fundamental element in enhancing road safety and protecting all road users. It also states that implementing the announced regulations is a shared responsibility between drivers and regulatory authorities.\n\nThe directorate considers compliance with these requirements the first line of defense in reducing the risks associated with truck traffic. It also contributes to raising the level of traffic discipline and achieving the highest standards of public safety on the roads.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEast–West Pipeline Shut Down as a Precaution Following Multiple Attacks (https://www.spa.gov.sa/en/N2674017)\nciteturn8search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Riyadh, September 11, 2026, SPA -- An official source at the Ministry of Energy stated that the East–West Pipeline in Riyadh and Madinah regions was subjected to multiple attacks on the morning of Thursday, September 10, 2026.\nEast–West Pipeline Shut Down as a Precaution Following Multiple Attacks\n\nImage: https://portalcdn.spa.gov.sa/backend/original/202609/M10777112.jpg\n\nRiyadh, September 11, 2026, SPA -- An official source at the Ministry of Energy stated that the East–West Pipeline in Riyadh and Madinah regions was subjected to multiple attacks on the morning of Thursday, September 10, 2026. The pipeline was shut down as a precautionary measure. The attacks resulted in a number of injuries, and medical care was provided to those affected.\nThe source said emergency and specialized technical teams responded immediately following the attacks, taking the necessary measures to secure the pipeline and assess its safety in line with approved safety procedures and emergency response plans, in coordination with the relevant authorities. Any further developments will be announced in due co